Given an integer x, the task is to find all pairs of positive integers (a, b) such that a - a % b = x, where a and b are integers.

Here's a straightforward approach using the concept of divisors and the property that any integer x can be expressed as a product of its prime factors. If we can find all prime factors of x, we can calculate all pairs (a, b) that satisfy the equation a - a (in which a and b are co-prime) and then validate them based on the equation.

```javascript
function findPairs(x) {
  // Iterate over all prime factors of x
  const primes = new Set([...Array.from(new Array(x + 1), (_, i) => i + 1)].reverse());

  // Prune the set based on the modulus equation
  const b = primes.values().next().value;
  const aMinusA = x - x % b;
  primes.delete(b);

  const pairs = [];
  for (const a of primes) {
    if (aMinusA % a === 0) {
      const ab = a * b;
      const pa = a * aMinusA / ab;
      const pb = ab - pa;
      pairs.push([a, pb]);
      pairs.push([pa, aMinusA / pa]);
    }
  }

  return pairs;
}

// Example usage
